:: Witch Hut Shake
You shake the hand Pruti held out for you and find yourself back in the hut as if you never left. Pruti gently pats your back and continues.
<br><br>
"What I need is a focus. Something I can channel the energy into to maintain a prolonged rift." A contemplative expression dresses Pruti's face as <<he>> thinks.
<br><br>
"Perhaps... something dark yet reflective. They may have something at the village. I need to prepare. I will meet you at the wreckage when you have something that works."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Witch Hut Trust]]>><</link>>

:: Pruti Shop Search
You search through the stalls yet don't find much of value. Your final stop is the artifact shop.
<br><br>
As you enter, the man behind the counter regards you with wary eyes. "What do you need."
<br><br>
You let the man know you are looking for an item that is dark and reflective. He thinks for a moment before going to the back room and returning a moment later.
<br><br>
"Is this something you would be interested in?" The man says, revealing an obsidian lens. It focuses the surrounding light into a rainbow gleam. Dark, reflective, this should be perfect.
<br><br>
"Well... this is a rare find but I could cut you a deal." The man lets out a crooked grin. "£10,000. This is a great deal you'd get nowhere else. We have a deal?"
<br><br>
<<if $money gte 1000000>>
	<<link [[Buy the lens|Lens Buy]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<span class="red">You don't have the funds for this purchase.</span>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Come back later|Desert Dock Shops]]>><</link>>

:: Lens Buy
You fork over the money to the artifact seller.
<br><br>
His crooked grin persists as he hands over the smooth obsidian lens. "Nice doin' business sweetheart."
<br><br>
You step back out of the tent and back to the scorching desert air.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Desert Dock Shops]]>><<set $portalquest to 2>><</link>>

:: Pruti Rift Setup
<<npc "Pruti">><<person1>>
As you enter the wreckage of the plane, you find Pruti. <<He>> is in <<his>> usual outfit, and seems to have modified the plane's interior. 
<br><br>
The plane's seats have been removed, leaving a metalic tube decorated with a new plinth that Pruti seems to have brought from elsewhere. 
<br><br>
Sensing your arrival, Pruti turns with a smile. "My doll, just in time. As you can see, I have refitted this vessel for our own needs. Do you have the focus?"
<br><br>
Pruti's probing shadowy arms feel up your form, grabbing the obsidian lens, pulling it to Pruti. <<He>> grips the surface and inspects it for a moment.
<br><br>
"A darkness that absorbs all light, yet reflects what needs reflected. This is perfect." Pruti places the lens onto the plinth.
<br><br>
The surroundings dim for a moment, before the light is reflected like a prism. The light freezes in the air, the space tearing into a purple rift.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Pruti Rift Setup 2]]>><<set $portalquest to 3>><</link>>

:: Pruti Rift Setup 2
"Well doll? Shall we?" Pruti holds out a hand. <<He>> holds you gently as you both step through the rift.
<br><br>
You emerge into the forest, but not the same forest. You can hear cars in the distance. It seems like you are on the outskirts of town.
<br><br>
This seems to be a small ruin hidden in the leaves. A small shrine built into a divot in the ground where what looks like a huge pearl sustains this end of the rift. 
<br><br>
Pruti winces and covers <<his>> sensitive ears from the loud noises of civilization. "Wow my doll, this place certainly is... loud. And the air here is quite sickening."
<br><br>
Despite the obvious discomfort, Pruti gives a shaky grin. "We should return home for now. I have something for you. Come."
<br><br>
<<link [[Follow Pruti back through the rift|Pruti Rift Setup 3]]>><<set $daily.riftisland to 1>><<set $daily.riftforest to 1>><</link>>

:: Pruti Rift Setup 3
You once again arrive on the island. As you exit the rift the air becomes thick. The portal begins to ooze a deep purple and black bile before winding and sealing.
<br><br>
Pruti notices your discomfort and confustion and begins to explain. "The energy that sustains the rift is limited. It uses the ambient magic that flows from the Earth."
<br><br>
<<He>> takes a moment to inspect the obsidian lens before turning back to you. "I would say the portal will likely only work once a day. Taking you between here and there."
<br><br>
Pruti turns to you and smirks. "How about a race home. Lets see if you can keep up."
<br><br>
<<link [[Race Pruti|Pruti Race]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Take your time|Race Result]]>><<set $prutiracelost to 1>><</link>>

